course: dictionary
lesson: 10128
title: Many meanings: thrash
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around a word, tells you which meaning fits. Thrash is a good example: it can mean a wild movement, a big win, or hitting someone.
explain: «If you get cramp in the water, roll onto your back, float, shout and wave for help, because panicking and thrashing tires you fast and you can swallow water.» Here thrashing means moving your arms and legs wildly in the water, not fighting. The clues are cramp, panicking and tires you fast.
explain: «We thrashed them 6-0.» In sports talk, thrashed means beat easily by a lot. Try your meaning in the sentence: «We beat them easily by a lot» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Thrash» can mean to move arms, legs or body around wildly and violently, like a fish thrashing on a hook.
fact: «Thrash» in sports talk means to beat a team easily by a lot. This use is informal.
fact: «Thrash» can also mean to beat or hit someone very hard many times. This is cruel and wrong.
fact: «Thrash out» means to talk about a problem until you solve it. Here thrash has nothing to do with hitting or moving.
fact: Check the clues before you choose a meaning: the words around a word tell you which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «Panicking and thrashing tires you fast in the water.» What does thrashing mean here? | Singing loudly for help | Floating calmly on your back | Walking slowly to the side | *Moving arms and legs wildly
exercise: «We thrashed them 6-0.» What does thrashed mean? | Hit them many times with a stick | Lost by a little | Cried loudly after the game | *Beat them easily by a lot
exercise: Ella and her friend need to «thrash out» the plan for the trip. What does thrash out mean? | Shout at each other until they are cross | Dance around wildly | *Talk until they solve the problem | Throw the plan away
test: «The fish began to thrash on the hook.» What does thrash mean? | Swim slowly away | Sing a happy song | *Move wildly and violently | Sleep quietly
test: Someone is thrashing about in deep water. What is the safe thing to do? | *Shout for a lifeguard and throw something that floats | Swim over and grab them | Ignore them and walk away | Jump straight in to help
exam: Which word could replace thrashed in «We thrashed them 6-0»? | Missed | *Beat easily | Hugged | Waved
